{"id":"5dae6487-1747-4d38-826a-f21b5f36872e","object":"chat.completion","created":1785025047,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    # Extract fields\\n    word_token_indices = case['word_token_indices']\\n    word_scores = case['word_scores']\\n    forced_words = case.get('forced_words', [])\\n    token_budget = case['token_budget']\\n\\n    n_words = len(word_token_indices)\\n    # Validate indices for forced_words\\n    for idx in forced_words:\\n        if not (0 <= idx < n_words):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Forced word index {idx} out of range\\\")\\n\\n    # Compute token counts per word\\n    token_counts = [len(tokens) for tokens in word_token_indices]\\n\\n    # Check feasibility of forced words\\n    forced_tokens = sum(token_counts[i] for i in forced_words)\\n    if forced_tokens > token_budget:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Forced words exceed token budget\\\")\\n\\n    # Remaining budget\\n    remaining = token_budget - forced_tokens\\n\\n    # Candidate words: not forced\\n    candidates = []\\n    for i in range(n_words):\\n        if i not in forced_words:\\n            candidates.append((i, word_scores[i], token_counts[i]))\\n\\n    # Sort by descending score, then ascending index (original position)\\n    candidates.sort(key=lambda x: (-x[1], x[0]))\\n\\n    # Greedy selection\\n    selected_set = set(forced_words)\\n    for idx, score, cnt in candidates:\\n        if cnt <= remaining:\\n            selected_set.add(idx)\\n            remaining -= cnt\\n\\n    # Build selected_words in original order\\n    selected_words = [i for i in range(n_words) if i in selected_set]\\n\\n    # Build retained_token_indices in original word order\\n    retained_token_indices = []\\n    for i in selected_words:\\n        retained_token_indices.extend(word_token_indices[i])\\n\\n    tokens_used = sum(token_counts[i] for i in selected_words)\\n\\n    return {\\n        'retained_token_indices': retained_token_indices,\\n        'selected_words': selected_words,\\n        'tokens_used': tokens_used\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to write a Python function solve(case) that implements the described task. The case has fields: word_token_indices (list of lists of ints), word_scores (list of floats), forced_words (list of ints), token_budget (int). Possibly other fields, but we should only use these. The output must have retained_token_indices (list of ints, the token indices that are kept), selected_words (list of ints, the word indices that are selected), tokens_used (int, total number of tokens used).\n\nThe algorithm: forced words must be selected first. Then among remaining words, sort by descending score, and for ties by original position (index). Then greedily add words if their token count fits within the remaining budget. Return the selected words in original order (not sorted order). The retained_token_indices should be the list of token indices from the selected words, in the order the tokens appear? The problem says \"Return words and tokens in original order\". So retained_token_indices should be the concatenation of the token indices from selected_words in the order of the words as they appear in the original list. Similarly selected_words should be the indices in original order.\n\nAlso check feasibility: sum tokens of forced_words must be <= token_budget. If not, raise ValueError.\n\nWe must not mutate input.\n\nImplementation: Extract fields. Validate that forced_words indices are within range of word_token_indices. Compute token count for each word. Check feasibility. Then create list of candidate words (indices not forced). Compute scores. Sort by (-score, index). Iterate, add if token count fits. Then build selected_words by filtering original indices that are forced or selected. Then compute retained_token_indices by flattening token lists in order of selected_words. Compute tokens_used as sum of lengths of those token lists.\n\nReturn dict with keys: retained_token_indices, selected_words, tokens_used.\n\nMake sure to handle case where no forced_words (empty list). Also if forced words exceed budget, raise ValueError.\n\nEdge cases: token_budget might be negative? Not expected but could raise.\n\nNo imports needed.\n\nThe output must be JSON-serializable, so lists and ints.\n\nNow, produce the code as a string to put into JSON.\n\nWrite the function with proper docstring maybe but not required.\n\nOutput exactly one JSON object with key \"implementation\" and value the Python source string, escaped.\n\nI'll produce the code."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1472,"completion_tokens":1002,"total_tokens":2474,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1408},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":506},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1408,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":64},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}